                <pb facs="0118" n="110" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg110"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/1264: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lima</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-19T18:00:00-04:00">December 19,
                            1939—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:17 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>106. Minister of Foreign Affairs has telegraphed the Peruvian diplomatic
                    representatives in Uruguay and Brazil to ascertain if those countries have
                    approved the Argentine draft. The Minister for Foreign Affairs personally favors
                    internment of belligerent vessels instead of action suggested in last paragraph
                    of Argentina draft. A definite reply has been promised by the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs as soon as he hears from Montevideo and Rio de Janeiro.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
